    "is_free": false,
    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You've Changed</strong> is an anomaly horror game in which you unravel a mystery behind the anomalies. Imagine <i>&quot;spot the difference&quot;</i> but scary. The game features 8-bit era inspired art and rotoscoped enemy animations.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Art Style and Graphics \ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Retro-inspired art style: You've Changed uses a limited, 54-color palette and renders at a resolution of just 320x180. The game is presented at 16:9 and scales crisply to modern resolutions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies are hand-crafted with\u00a0<strong>silky-smooth, rotoscoped</strong> animations.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/1f94948251c161ba9fa0746b9c3bf06b.poster.avif?t=1753297007\" width=616 height=292 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/1f94948251c161ba9fa0746b9c3bf06b.webm?t=1753297007\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/1f94948251c161ba9fa0746b9c3bf06b.mp4?t=1753297007\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Gameplay \ud83c\udfae</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Over <strong>300+ anomalies</strong> across 4 locations - unravel the mystery in story mode or find every anomaly in arcade mode.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>5 increasingly devious difficulties</strong> - newcomers can increase difficulty at their own pace. Fans of the genre can enjoy extremely challenging difficulty levels they can sink their teeth into.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Customizable jump scare intensity</strong> - you can lower the intensity or completely disable jump scares. You can instead enjoy the game as a pure, psychological horror.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/533b1c08710706d8d69a4d91b74ce82f.poster.avif?t=1753297007\" width=616 height=346 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/533b1c08710706d8d69a4d91b74ce82f.webm?t=1753297007\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/533b1c08710706d8d69a4d91b74ce82f.mp4?t=1753297007\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>(illustrative example only - in-game, there is a maximum of one anomaly per room at any given time)</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Fair Anomaly Initiation Rules (F.A.I.R.) spawn system\u00a0\u2696\ufe0f</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The <strong>F.A.I.R. spawn system</strong> is a finely tuned balance and difficulty manager. </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The system has been <i>meticulously balanced</i> across all difficulty levels to spawn challenging anomalies at the optimum frequency.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Anomalies deal more damage, more frequently on higher difficulties. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >On lower difficulties, anomalies &quot;decay&quot; if the player is struggling to find them, preventing failed runs from one unnoticed anomaly.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Anomalies don't spawn when the level timer is almost up, they don't spawn while you are learning the rooms, and they never spawn when you are looking at them. <strong>F.A.I.R. is fair!</strong> </p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/2bb4b8e4cae56dbc9718eece953106f5.poster.avif?t=1753297007\" width=616 height=250 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/2bb4b8e4cae56dbc9718eece953106f5.webm?t=1753297007\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/2bb4b8e4cae56dbc9718eece953106f5.mp4?t=1753297007\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Reporting-In-Progress (R.I.P.) damage prevention system\u00a0\ud83e\udea6</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The <strong>R.I.P. damage prevention system</strong> avoids frustrating losses and gives you the opportunity to clutch victory from the jaws of defeat. </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >R.I.P. prevents you from <u>dying</u> when a report is being made.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Successful reports <strong>block damage &amp; death</strong> but if you are wrong\u2026 you will only have delayed the inevitable \ud83d\udc80</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/494c5b1129e4233786a0eae56c20bb72.poster.avif?t=1753297007\" width=616 height=346 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/494c5b1129e4233786a0eae56c20bb72.webm?t=1753297007\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/494c5b1129e4233786a0eae56c20bb72.mp4?t=1753297007\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Story \ud83d\udcd6</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What caused the anomalies? Who or what is behind them? Why do they appear at certain locations? <u>Find the answer</u> without succumbing to their power.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You've Changed</strong> features a mysterious story mode and a highly re-playable arcade mode. Notes and extras are available in a separate Lore menu.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556110/extras/694dcb86fc05c38eb2ff1536bd2a60e0.avif?t=1753297007\" width=614 height=338 /></span></p>",
